{
  "title": "SKY130 PFET f_T",
  "group": "SKY130 transistors",
  "description": "SKY130 PFET bandwidth / f_T (fixture-free |h21|), with an optional width sweep",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 170,
        "y": -118,
        "title": "SKY130 PFET f_T — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "A single PFET MP1 has source/body at VDD = 1.8 V (VDD1),",
          "drain at 0 V (VD1) and gate at 0.6 V (VG1), so Vgs = -1.2 V.",
          "The AC sweep (10 MHz -> 1 THz) gives current gain h21;",
          "f_T is where |h21| = 1.",
          "",
          "A width sweep (MP1.w_um 0.5 -> 8 um) ships pre-configured",
          "in the sweep-parameters pane but starts OFF. Enable it to",
          "plot f_T vs width: f_T ~ gm / (2*pi*Cgg), and gm and Cgg",
          "both scale with width, so f_T stays nearly flat.",
          "",
          "Set MP1.l_um = 0.5 and re-run to see f_T drop -- f_T falls",
          "steeply with channel length, at every width."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "instances": {
